WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.620
How do you understand the number 462?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.560
I mean we know it's 462.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.220
But how do we look at it in terms of its digits?

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.680
In every number each digit you see has a place value.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:23.000
And that depends entirely on where the digit is placed or positioned.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.640
Here, the digit two is in the ones place.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.420
While six is in the tens place and four in the hundreds place.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.040
With the help of place value, let's try to break this number down.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:42.440
As four lies in the hundreds place, we can write four times 100.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.840
As six is in the tens place,

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.880
we add six times ten to this.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.840
And as two is in the ones place we add two times one.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.800
That's how we understand the number 462.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.540
400+ 60+2

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.780
But what if we have a decimal point in the number?

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.720
Say a number like 462.351.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.000
How do we understand this number?

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.320
It's simple!

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.100
The digits that appear before the decimal point,

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.640
work just like this one.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:21.320
It will be four times 100, plus six times ten, plus two times one.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.180
But what is the place value of the digits after the decimal point?

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.580
The first digit after the decimal point in this case is three.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.520
Is it in the tens place?

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.440
Not tens, its tenths place.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.080
So it's value would be three times 1 by 10

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.680
or three tenths we can say.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.740
The second digit to the right of the decimal point

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.060
which is five is in the hundredths place.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:53.860
It means that its value will be five times 1 by 100.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.760
The third digit to the right of the decimal point,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.580
which is one, is said to be in the thousandths place.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.840
So we add one multiplied by one by one thousand.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.340
If you add these six values,

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:12.100
you will get four hundred sixty-two point three five one.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.300
Decimals are just another way of representing fractions.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.080
This number can also be written as

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.520
four hundred and sixty two thousand three hundred and fifty one

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.380
by one thousand.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.400
As they are another way of representing fractions,

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.000
they are called decimal fractions.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.060
Notice that as we move towards the right

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.580
the place value reduces to one tenth of the previous place value.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:45.120
100 by 10 is 10, 10 by 10 is 1 and so on...

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.040
Here,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.760
462 is called the integral part of the number.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:53.900
And 351 is called the decimal part.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.120
There are many things we need to understand about decimal fractions.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.180
Their types, ways to compare them,

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.800
operations on them and many more concepts.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.740
We will understand these in the next few videos.

